  "verbalization": "Pestaloficiol A appears to have a target relationship with SCCH-26 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Pestaloficiol A acts as a target for RXF 631, which in turn is targeted by Malvidin 3-rutinoside-5-glucoside and another compound, (2R,10S,12R,16R,18R)-6,7-dihydroxy-8-(hydroxymethyl)-4,18-dimethyl-14-nonyl-16-prop-1-en-2-yl-9,13,15,19-tetraoxahexacyclo[12.4.1.01,11.02,6.08,10.012,16]nonadec-3-en-5-one. Both of these compounds ultimately target SCCH-26, indicating a potential pathway where Pestaloficiol A may influence the biological activity of these molecules, leading to effects on SCCH-26. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a possible mechanism involving the interaction of Pestaloficiol A with a series of compounds that modulate SCCH-26. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, but the core mechanism remains that Pestaloficiol A may act as a mediator in the targeting of SCCH-26 through these downstream compounds.",
